# Spoken labels (ISZE chat + shared UI)


## Forbidden → say instead

| Do not say | Say |
|---|---|
| **Mode A / Mode B** (any form) | **shared / external** vs **internal / private**. Never use Mode A or Mode B in chat or in files Jerome opens. |
| wallet / wallet € / parts wallet | **parts billed** vs **target spend per truck** (or “what we billed” vs “GPS target € per unit”) |
| street / street fills / street index | **OEM peer retail** / **reference dealer price** / **price index** (shop ÷ reference dealer price) |
| **sell-out / sell out / sellout** | **sales to dealer** (Jerome has asked repeatedly — this is a banned word, not a style preference) |
| **Book B** (any form, bare or glossed) | **the price list** / **a price revision**. Jerome does not use “Book B” — do not introduce it, do not gloss it, do not ask which initiative it is. Pricing work is a **separate track**: SPA work plus a price revision, timing owned by Jerome. |
| ×1.785 with no English | One sentence first: ISZE list × 1.40 to the dealer × 1.275 to the customer price we use as **reference dealer price**. The factor may then appear in a footnote. |

Filenames that contain a banned word may be quoted **once** in a footnote.

JSON field names (`peer_street_eur`, `wallet_eur`) may stay in pipeline code. Labels to Jerome and in dashboards must not.

## Talk in margins, never in factors

**Jerome, 2026-09-17:** *"please work with margins like I do not factors, I asked this before?"*

He has asked more than once. This is a hard rule.

| Do not write | Write instead |
|---|---|
| class factor 0.47 / `class_factor` | **53% margin** |
| factor band 0.70–1.35 (launch) | **margin band** — state as margin, e.g. 30% to −35% vs class, or as a price multiple with the margin beside it |
| `qingling_overlap_gm: 0.45` | **45% margin on parts a Chinese equivalent exists for** |
| `no_overlap_gm: 0.60` | **60% margin where it cannot be followed** |
| `CIS factor_flat: 0.40` | **60% margin, flat across the catalogue** |
| `source_discount: J 0.62 / T 0.611` | state the **margin** it implies, once, then the code |
| "1 − class_factor" | just the margin |

**Why:** the factor is the **divisor**; the margin is the **decision**. `SP = FOB / factor`, so `margin = 1 − factor`. Jerome thinks, quotes and negotiates in margin. A pack he reads that says "factor 0.47" makes him do the arithmetic himself, and it hides the fact that a factor *is* a margin someone set.

**Where the code may keep its own name:** JSON/YAML field names (`class_factor`, `qingling_overlap_gm`) stay as they are in files — same convention as `peer_street_eur`. Only the **label he reads** is a margin. If a factor must be shown for traceability, show the margin first and the factor in a footnote.

**This extends to the class codes.** C / D / F / J / M / P / T / V are IML's letters and carry no commercial meaning to him on their own. Write the margin: "class C (53% margin)", not "class C (factor 0.47)".

## Talk plainly

Default to plain business English. Say “trucks in service”, not parc; “what we billed”, not capture; “dealer price”, not a bare formula. Keep a real term only when it is the clearest word for the thing, and gloss it the first time. No shorthand that only an agent would invent.

## Packs

First time a formula or internal code appears in a pack, add one plain English sentence. Then the code is fine.

## Bot English — never in chat or shared packs

loss function, grain, cartoon, brain, SPAR, ship-gate, harness, Mode A, Mode B.

## Pricing words (moved from isze-pricing-no-street-ui.mdc, 2026-10-05)

Jerome asked to **stop saying "street fills"**. He also asked to **stop saying sell-out**. Chat and shared UI use **sales to dealer** and **%GM**.

| Forbidden in chat + shared UI | Say instead |
|---|---|
| street / street fills / street € | **OEM peer retail** |
| sell-out / sellout / reference sell-out / dealer sell-out | **sales to dealer** (StD) for DB→dealer volume; **%GM** for commercial terms |
| street index | **price index** (shop ÷ our GM-grossed list, if he asked for that view) |
| undercut street | **below the price the dealer works with** |
| fill the street | **get OEM peer retail prices** |
| ×1.40 × 1.275 / ×1.785 as the working label | **%GM** — do not brief him in markup factors |

JSON / code field names (`peer_street_eur`, `street_index`, `sellout_qty`) may stay for pipeline compatibility — **spoken and written labels to Jerome and in dashboards must not say street or sell-out**.
